  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef wants to make a feast. In order to do that, he needs a lot of different ingredients. Each ingredient has a certain tastiness; the tastiness of each ingredient may be any positive integer. Initially, for each tastiness between KKK and K+N−1K+N-1K+N−1 (inclusive), Chef has an infinite supply of ingredients with this tastiness.\n\nThe ingredients have a special property: any two of them can be mixed to create a new ingredient. If the original ingredients had tastiness xxx and yyy (possibly x=yx = yx=y), the new ingredient has tastiness x+yx+yx+y. The ingredients created this way may be used to mix other ingredients as well. Chef is free to mix ingredients in any way he chooses any number of times.\n\nLet's call a tastiness vvv (v&gt;0v \\gt 0v&gt;0) unreachable if there is no way to obtain an ingredient with tastiness vvv; otherwise, tastiness vvv is reachable. Chef wants to make ingredients with all reachable values of tastiness and he would like to know the number of unreachable values. Help him solve this problem. Since the answer may be large, compute it modulo 1,000,000,0071,000,000,0071,000,000,007 (109+710^9+7109+7).\n\nNote that there is an infinite number of reachable values of tastiness, but it can be proven that the number of unreachable values is always finite for N≥2N \\ge 2N≥2.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\le T \\le 10^51≤T≤105",
      "2≤N≤10182 \\le N \\le 10^{18}2≤N≤1018",
      "1≤K≤10181 \\le K \\le 10^{18}1≤K≤1018",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (20 points):** N=2N = 2N=2"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing one integer — the number of unreachable values of tastiness, modulo 1,000,000,0071,000,000,0071,000,000,007.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n2 1\n3 3",
        "output": "0\n2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1: It is possible to obtain ingredients with all values of tastiness.\nExample case 2: Ingredients with tastiness 111 and 222 cannot be made."
      }
    ]
  },
